From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:56:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] linux: one context per hart online by default

With MULTITHREAD above 1, the port linux runs MULTITHREAD contexts,
unless its first argument M<n> sets another count. It now runs one
context per hart online by default, as sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN)
counts them, MULTITHREAD at most, with a warning above it, as the port
of rv32-sim/apps/coremark of the FonTamSOC runs them on underLineOS.

With the MULTITHREAD of 16 of the previous patch, a single-hart system
thus runs one context rather than 16, each of which would run the
iterations which take about 10 seconds to one hart. The argument M<n>
still sets the count, 16 at most.

Upstream: N/A, specific to the FonTamSOC
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
---
 linux/core_portme.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/linux/core_portme.c b/linux/core_portme.c
index 2f07490..b5cf7eb 100755
--- a/linux/core_portme.c
+++ b/linux/core_portme.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 */ 
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include "coremark.h"
 #if CALLGRIND_RUN
 #include <valgrind/callgrind.h>
@@ -185,6 +186,20 @@ void portable_init(core_portable *p, int *argc, char *argv[])
 	ee_printf("ERROR! Main has no argc, but SEED_METHOD defined to SEED_ARG!\n");
 #endif
 	
+#if (MULTITHREAD>1)
+	/* One context per hart online, MULTITHREAD at most, as the port of
+	 * rv32-sim/apps/coremark of the FonTamSOC runs them on underLineOS;
+	 * the argument M<n> below sets another count.
+	 */
+	{
+		long n=sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN);
+		if (n>MULTITHREAD) {
+			ee_printf("WARNING! sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN)>MULTITHREAD!\n");
+			n=MULTITHREAD;
+		}
+		default_num_contexts=(n>0)?(ee_u32)n:1;
+	}
+#endif
 #if (MULTITHREAD>1) && (SEED_METHOD==SEED_ARG)
 	{
 		int nargs=*argc,i;
